+# FlyWeb: release after 3.2.2 (softmac `seguridad/siguiente-3`), V8 fix 1faf157db2 (crbug 585869521), ported from the M159 merge
+
+SEGURIDAD-PORTES-33, 23-11-2026 (softmac `FlyWeb/seguridad/siguiente-3/brave-core/0001`). **Not merged to V8 15.6
+upstream yet**: ported from the M159 merge 1faf157db2 (V8 15.9.128.34, bugs 587680279 and 585869521; cherry-pick of
+5796f2ed1d from main). Severity not published; it is a sandbox escape (a write outside the V8 sandbox).
+
+- `JSLocale` `ApplyOptionsToTag` passed the tag to `icu::LocaleBuilder::setLanguageTag()` with a
+  `static_cast<int32_t>` of the `Utf8Value` length. With an in-sandbox corrupted string the UTF-8 length can be
+  0xFFFFFFFF, which truncates to -1, and ICU then writes a NUL one byte before a static buffer, outside the sandbox. Now
+  the tag goes through `String::ToStdString()`, whose length is bounded by `SBXCHECK_LE(length, String::kMaxLength)`.
+- That bound is the 15.6 merge of 133ba8e4a90 (crbug 579314138), already in `patches/v8/src-objects-string.cc.patch`, so
+  the fix is complete on our base. `js-locale.cc` is byte-identical in 15.6.75.66 and upstream before the fix; no other
+  `patches/v8` file touches it. `mjsunit.status`: the same `[PASS, SLOW]` line as upstream, in the 15.6 list (the context
+  differs). Plus the test `sandbox/regress/regress-585869521.js`.
+
+**Cache epoch:** this changes the Intl builtins, so **`kFlyWebCacheEpoch` 40 -> 41**, once, for the release that carries
+`siguiente-3`. Any other V8 change added to that release is covered by this same bump.
+
+To check (D8-LINUX): `d8` with the sandbox testing flags, mjsunit `sandbox/regress/regress-585869521` and `intl*/*`.
+
